/E (In an artistic context, Vette investigates what remains when representation is gradually reduced to its essential elements. Each work begins with a real mountain, but moves beyond traditional landscape painting. Through layers of marks, text fragments, geographical references, and abstraction, the paintings become less concerned with depicting a place and more concerned with revealing its presence.)
/Pg 12 0 R
/K [2]
>>
endobj
