/P 54 0 R
/E (In a cultural context, Vette reflects on the way we organize and interpret the natural world. Mountains exist independently of us, yet our relationship with them is mediated through systems of classification, protected areas, tourism, cartography, and language. The series questions how much of a place belongs to the landscape itself and how much belongs to the frameworks we build around it.)
/Pg 12 0 R
/K [5]
>>
endobj
