/P 54 0 R
/E (In a personal context, Vette represents an exercise in observation and reduction. Rather than adding information, the process seeks to remove it. The works emerge through a gradual distillation of form, allowing memory, structure, and presence to replace description. The mountain becomes less an object to depict and more a trace to contemplate.)
/Pg 12 0 R
/K [8]
>>
endobj
87 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 54 0 R
/E (In a time characterized by excess information, Vette proposes a different approach: slowing down, observing carefully, and allowing meaning to emerge through reduction rather than accumulation. The series invites the viewer to consider what remains when the need to explain, classify, and describe begins to fade.)
/Pg 12 0 R
/K [9]
>>
endobj
