/E (Born in Trentino, Italy, in 1979, Claudio Gobber grew up in the mountain valleys of Primiero and Vanoi. These landscapes continue to shape his way of observing the world and influence an artistic practice centered on attention, reduction, and presence.)
/Pg 17 0 R
/K [0]
>>
endobj
145 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 59 0 R
/E (Working across painting, sculpture, photography, and design, Gobber explores the traces left behind by contemporary life. His work investigates themes such as dignity, adaptation, memory, love, loss, and the relationship between people and the systems they create.)
/Pg 17 0 R
/K [1]
>>
endobj
